Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Declare team sets by subject, and read their names from
 precedent.json

Three changes, all of them upstream groundwork for splitting the private
team catalogue by subject rather than by where the rules were written.

INSTALL.md: a repo declares as many team sets as its work needs, and that
is the ordinary case. Adds the table that answers "which ones?" from the
kind of work the repo is for, and states the pattern under it -- a set
about a KIND OF WORK is declared by everyone who does that work, whatever
team they are on; a set about running a kind of repository is declared
only by repositories of that kind.

templates/nontechnical-document-project/AGENTS.md: the session-start
`add_repo` instruction named one set outright, so declaring a second one
silently required editing two files that nothing kept in agreement. It
now reads the set names out of precedent.json. The failure mode it
removes is not an error but a session that quietly resolves fewer
practices than the config promises.

templates/nontechnical-document-project/precedent.json: declares the two
new subject-scoped sets, and says why the repo-mechanics set is
deliberately NOT declared -- not declaring a set is the cheap way to say
"this does not apply here"; a not_binding entry per slug is the expensive
one. Also corrects this file's own description of that set as "code-repo
conventions", which was never true: over half its rules are about
writing, and they were unreachable from a document project because of it.

doc_lint on INSTALL.md: 40 findings before, 40 after -- a pre-existing
backlog, nothing added.

