Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Close split-team-sets-by-subject with the sort and the
 migration it used

The sort is done, from a session holding all five sets plus this repo --
the route attach-private-sources named, working as written.

Records what the split actually found, not just that it happened: 19 of
40 practices in the maintainers' set were about something other than
maintaining a repository; three further moves were proposed and REVERSED
on reading the rules rather than their slugs, one of which says in its
own text that it is not team policy; and the two practices that fire on
every turn of every session were reachable only by repositories that
also took twenty-odd rules about syncs and gates.

Also records the migration path for repos still on the old declaration,
since that is the part a future session needs and the item did not have:
the two-step move spec/MOVING_PRACTICES.md prescribes, applied 19 times,
so every moved practice keeps a deduplicated file in the old set naming
where it went. A repo that has not updated its precedent.json resolves
fewer practices and can see, by name, which set now holds each one.

Leaves catalogue-carries-stories' team-shadows-universal duplicate to
practice-consistency-across-team-repos, where it belongs, and leaves item
7 parked -- nothing here produced two sources that disagree.

