From 1b85084b61e336d7b10774c77bb783d609c93266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Morgan F <morgan@westegg.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:50:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Correct the catalogue-carries-stories note: it is not a
 duplicate

I recorded it as a team copy shadowing a live universal one, for
practice-consistency-across-team-repos to drop. Reading the practice
file rather than the slug overlap says otherwise, and it says so in its
own Story: it was deduplicated on 2026-09-07 and re-activated the same
day.

The reason is mechanical. A source repo consumes no catalogue, so
universal's copy never reaches a set like that one, and
precedent_check.py gates every check on its practice being in force
THERE. Deduplicating it did not defer enforcement to universal -- it
switched enforcement off. The same-slug copy is the mechanism by which a
source set puts a universal rule in force on its own catalogue.

Also attaches this as the counter-example to
practice-consistency-across-team-repos' own "a copy is usually the bug"
premise, because a reconcile tool built on that premise would make this
exact mistake automatically and silently: same slug, active in two
sources, promote and delete. The distinguishing question is whether the
lower source actually RESOLVES the higher one -- which the resolver can
answer and a similarity score cannot.

